  "synthesis": "The common thread is inferring and testing how regulatory or metabolic organization changes between conditions, using mechanistic or network-level descriptors. Kinetic ensembles constrained by multi-omics in BRCA1-deficient ovarian cancer predict 28 enzyme vulnerabilities. An eleven-variable Nrf1/Nrf2 model identifies a bistable persistent-stress attractor. Network topology modelling attributes recovery of heterogeneous expression during self-renewal to feedback loops. Causal discovery on Visium data separates local from neighbor-derived effects in liver senescence. CellStressDB aggregates 131 transcriptomic studies across nine physical-stress classes. A benchmark of six drug-perturbation resources finds limited cross-source concordance, which tempers confidence in transcriptional-response inference. The new element is pairing mechanistic and causal models with explicit reproducibility assessment.",
